# Did anybody look? One row per question a document was asked about its own diligence, carrying
# what it answered.
#
# The row that makes an empty table readable
#   Without it an empty table is ambiguous in the worst way. A filing with no couplings has either a
#   stack of independent layers or nobody who looked; a fusion with no eliminations has either no
#   double counting or no search for it. Those are opposite claims and the tall table renders them
#   identically. The search element is where the difference lives.
#
# The answer decides which arithmetic is owed
#   That is what raises this above bookkeeping. `none` or `notApplicable` on a fusion: the composed
#   figure must equal the sum of its converted parts exactly. `unmeasured`: no equality is owed at
#   all, and a checker reporting one is reporting about nothing.
#
# A null `answer` is not an absence here
#   It means the document actually filed the thing (real couplings, real eliminations), so the
#   search question is answered by the content.
#
# The two members are files
#   That is what makes this union honest. Build both arms inline against their base tables and
#   every caller wanting one kind of search filters on the `looked_for` string this file invented:
#   a union taken back apart by string comparison at every call site, and callers that give up and
#   read the base table instead. A union whose members are not files is a union nobody can compose
#   half of.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings and asrt:Fusion/asrt:eliminations, each with its pm:absent.
SELECT cs.filing, 'couplings between layers' AS looked_for, '(the stack)' AS about,
       cs.answer, cs.note
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) cs
UNION ALL
SELECT es.composition, 'double counting across parts', es.composed_layer,
       es.answer, es.note
FROM (
    :compose(eliminations/searched.sqlc)
) es
